From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pet0203 <Pet0203@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: unprepare the GPU clocks across system suspend

On MediaTek SoCs (MT8192 here) the GPU clock's parent, mfgpll, is a PLL
that is powered in .prepare/.unprepare, not in .enable/.disable. The
GPU_PM_CLK_DIS system-suspend path only calls clk_disable(), so mfgpll
stays prepared, and therefore running, for the whole of suspend.

A running PLL keeps the SPM from dropping the 26 MHz bus clock, so the SoC
never reaches its deep suspend state and never asserts AP_IN_SLEEP_L. The
ChromeOS EC waits for that signal: when it does not arrive, the EC's
sleep-hang detection fires ("Detected sleep hang! Waking host up!") and
wakes the machine a few seconds after it went to sleep.

Use clk_disable_unprepare() on suspend and clk_prepare_enable() on resume
so the PLL really stops.

This is for v7.3 and older, and does not apply to v7.4, which reworks the
driver's clock handling into panfrost_clks_enable() and
panfrost_clks_disable(). The rework does not fix the problem. The suspend
path there does call clk_disable_unprepare(), but panfrost_clk_init() now
holds a second clk_prepare() of its own on each clock, so the prepare count
never reaches zero and the PLL is still left running across suspend. That
is from reading v7.4-rc3, not from a test on it; v7.4 needs its own
version of this fix.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_device.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_device.c
index d0a23c51b..8aa435cac 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_device.c
@@ -508,12 +508,12 @@ static int panfrost_device_resume(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	if (pfdev->comp->pm_features & BIT(GPU_PM_CLK_DIS)) {
-		ret = clk_enable(pfdev->clock);
+		ret = clk_prepare_enable(pfdev->clock);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_clk;
 
 		if (pfdev->bus_clock) {
-			ret = clk_enable(pfdev->bus_clock);
+			ret = clk_prepare_enable(pfdev->bus_clock);
 			if (ret)
 				goto err_bus_clk;
 		}
@@ -527,10 +527,10 @@ static int panfrost_device_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 err_resume:
 	if (pfdev->comp->pm_features & BIT(GPU_PM_CLK_DIS) && pfdev->bus_clock)
-		clk_disable(pfdev->bus_clock);
+		clk_disable_unprepare(pfdev->bus_clock);
 err_bus_clk:
 	if (pfdev->comp->pm_features & BIT(GPU_PM_CLK_DIS))
-		clk_disable(pfdev->clock);
+		clk_disable_unprepare(pfdev->clock);
 err_clk:
 	if (pfdev->comp->pm_features & BIT(GPU_PM_VREG_OFF))
 		dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
@@ -548,9 +548,9 @@ static int panfrost_device_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	if (pfdev->comp->pm_features & BIT(GPU_PM_CLK_DIS)) {
 		if (pfdev->bus_clock)
-			clk_disable(pfdev->bus_clock);
+			clk_disable_unprepare(pfdev->bus_clock);
 
-		clk_disable(pfdev->clock);
+		clk_disable_unprepare(pfdev->clock);
 	}
 
 	if (pfdev->comp->pm_features & BIT(GPU_PM_VREG_OFF))
